    {
      "skill_id": "de-a1-010",
      "title": "Dative forms in fixed expressions and verb frames",
      "explanation": "The dative is the case of the indirect object and of some fixed patterns. Dative articles: dem for masculine and neuter nouns, der for feminine nouns, den (plus -n on the noun) for plurals. Learn the dative in frequent chunks: mit dem Bus, mit der Freundin, mit dem Auto, and in verb frames such as helfen (jemandem helfen), gehören (Das Buch gehört dem Kind) and gefallen. The preposition mit always takes the dative.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Ich fahre mit dem Bus.",
          "en": "I travel by bus."
        },
        {
          "de": "Anna hilft der Frau.",
          "en": "Anna helps the woman."
        },
        {
          "de": "Das Buch gehört dem Kind.",
          "en": "The book belongs to the child."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["GOETHE-A1"],
